# d3-check rule

1. **Reuse before adding.** Search existing logic (d3utils, timers, controller, pycore); extend or parameterize; no second implementation of same behavior.
2. **No redundant definitions.** No duplicate constant/helper/wrapper. Literals → `providor.app_constants`; use existing helpers.
3. **Pycore direct; no secondary encapsulation.** Import from `pycore.*`; no `providor.common_imports`. One-shot: `timers.timer_manager.submit_one_shot` + **`timers.one_shot_tasks.do_*`**. **share**: `share/values` (data only), `share/common` (shared functions/base); no run_/do_; no dirs like data/store/cache (gitignore-prone). See `docs/PROJECT_STANDARDS.md` §1.3.
4. **Constants/config.** Literals → `providor.app_constants`; structured → `config`. No new literals in feature modules.
5. **Threads.** No mutual blocking; event center only; init at startup; one-shot via timer_manager; native Thread. See `docs/THREAD_BUS_AND_REGISTRY.md`.
6. **New standards.** Add to (1) `.cursor/rules` (2) `.cursor/skills` (3) `AGENTS.md`; no duplicate; canonical = PROJECT_STANDARDS.md.
7. **Prompts.** d3-check prompts → `pyapps/d3-check/.prompts/`.
8. **Every edit.** Check: redundant → merge; similar code → extend; architecture → fit event center, CONFIG. See `.cursor/skills/d3-check/SKILL.md` §10–11.
9. **Exception handling.** Remove unnecessary try/except. Keep only when required for basic program operation: websocket/network, task thread (so one failure does not kill the process), Tk lifecycle (`tk.TclError`), queue (`queue.Full`/`Empty`), COM/OS, signal handlers. See `.cursor/skills/d3-check/SKILL.md` §11.
10. **Imports.** All imports at file top. Exception: optional third-party at module level (`try: import x except ImportError: x = None`). Do not use lazy import to avoid cycles; fix circular references by architecture (split module, dependency injection, or shared layer). See `docs/PROJECT_STANDARDS.md` §6.1.
11. **No getter-style runtime detection.** Do not use `hasattr`/`callable`/`getattr(..., None)` to decide at runtime whether to call an API. Rely on type/API contract at code level and call directly (e.g. control.Exists(), control.GetChildren()). Guarantee availability by architecture; no defensive runtime checks for method presence. See `docs/PROJECT_STANDARDS.md` §6.2.
12. **Flow library & state ownership.** Flow 开关与每步/节点状态只由**单一流程类库** `d3utils.rosbot_flow*` 持有（见 `docs/FLOW_STATE_OWNERSHIP_DESIGN.md`、`docs/FLOW_ARCHITECTURE_DIRECTORY.md`、`docs/FLOW_IMPLEMENTATION_PROGRESS.md`）。Tick 入口 `rosbot_task_processor.process_task()` 只读 `rosbot_flow_state` 并调用 `tick_bn_only_flow()` / `tick_flow_master()`；controller / timers / UI（如 `controller/login_try_screenshot_controller.py`、`timers/one_shot_tasks.py`、各 panel）一律视为**第三方调用方**：只能调用 flow 层公开的函数，不得自建或直接读写 flow_master/bn_only/BN 步骤等流程状态。
13. **Code language & i18n (PROJECT_STANDARDS §11).** Code (comments, docstrings, log text, names) in English. User-facing strings via i18n only; constants (match keywords, config keys) unchanged.
